data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" Rust enforces memory safety at compile time. If code compiles in Rust, it is guaranteed free of data races and null-","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":"pointer dereferences.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Performance and Execution Model\n\nPerformance is a critical differentiator among the three languages:\n\n*   ","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":"**Python** is an interpreted language (executed via bytecode through the Pytesseract or CPython interpreter). It is notoriously","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" slower than compiled languages. Furthermore, CPython utilizes a Global Interpreter Lock (GIL), which prevents multiple native threads from executing Python","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" bytecodes at once, hindering CPU-bound multithreading. However, Python bridges this gap by serving as a wrapper for high","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

